{"file_path": "WEBSOCKET_AND_API_DOCUMENTATION.md", "initial_content": "# WebSocket & Complete API Documentation

## Overview
Comprehensive documentation for the Arkan platform API, including REST endpoints and WebSocket real-time communication.

---

## 🔌 WebSocket Integration

### Connection
```
URL: ws://localhost:4000
Authentication: Firebase ID Token
Transports: WebSocket, Polling (fallback)
```

### Frontend Usage

#### Auto-Connection
```typescript
// WebSocket automatically connects when user authenticates
// Handled by WebSocketProvider in app/providers.tsx
import { WebSocketProvider } from '@/components/websocket-provider';

<WebSocketProvider>
  {children}
</WebSocketProvider>
```

#### Manual Control
```typescript
import { useWebSocketConnection } from '@/hooks/use-websocket';

function MyComponent() {
  const { isConnected, isAuthenticated, connect, disconnect } = useWebSocketConnection();

  return (
    <div>
      Status: {isConnected ? 'Connected' : 'Disconnected'}
      <button onClick={connect}>Connect</button>
      <button onClick={disconnect}>Disconnect</button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### Listen to Events
```typescript
import { useWebSocketEvent, SocketEvents } from '@/hooks/use-websocket';

function MyComponent() {
  useWebSocketEvent(SocketEvents.PROJECT_CREATED, (project) => {
    console.log('New project created:', project);
    // React Query cache is automatically invalidated
  });

  return <div>Listening for real-time updates...</div>;
}
```

#### Real-Time Projects
```typescript
import { useWebSocketProjects } from '@/hooks/use-websocket';

function ProjectsList() {
  // Automatically invalidates React Query cache on project changes
  useWebSocketProjects();

  const { projects } = useProjects(); // Auto-updates in real-time!

  return <div>{/* Projects list */}</div>;
}
```

#### Connection Status UI
```typescript
import { WebSocketStatus, WebSocketDot } from '@/components/websocket-status';

// Full status badge
<WebSocketStatus />

// Simple indicator dot
<WebSocketDot />
```

---

## 📡 WebSocket Events

### Server → Client Events

| Event | Description | Payload |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| `connect` | Connected to server | - |
| `disconnect` | Disconnected from server | `reason: string` |
| `authenticated` | Successfully authenticated | `{ userId, email }` |
| `auth_error` | Authentication failed | `{ message }` |
| `project:created` | Project created | `Project` object |
| `project:updated` | Project updated | `Project` object |
| `project:deleted` | Project deleted | `{ projectId }` |
| `user:updated` | User profile updated | `User` object |
| `notification` | New notification | `Notification` object |
| `typing:start` | User started typing | `{ userId, ...data }` |
| `typing:stop` | User stopped typing | `{ userId, ...data }` |

### Client → Server Events

| Event | Description | Payload |
|-------|-------------|---------|
| `typing:start` | Notify others of typing | `any` |
| `typing:stop` | Stop typing notification | `any` |

### Example: Typing Indicators
```typescript
import { useTypingIndicator } from '@/hooks/use-websocket';

function ChatInput() {
  const { typingUsers, startTyping, stopTyping } = useTypingIndicator();

  const handleChange = (e) => {
    startTyping({ room: 'chat-1' });
    // ... handle input
  };

  const handleBlur = () => {
    stopTyping({ room: 'chat-1' });
  };

  return (
    <>
      {typingUsers.length > 0 && <div>Someone is typing...</div>}
      <input onChange={handleChange} onBlur={handleBlur} />
    </>
  );
}
```

---

## 🌐 REST API Endpoints

### Base URL
```
http://localhost:4000/api/v1
```

### Authentication
All protected endpoints require Firebase ID Token:
```
Authorization: Bearer <firebase_id_token>
```

---

## 🔐 Authentication Endpoints

### POST `/auth/signup`
Create a new user account.

**Request:**
```json
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "displayName": "John Doe"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "user": {
    "id": "user_id",
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "displayName": "John Doe"
  }
}
```

### POST `/auth/logout`
Logout and revoke tokens. **(Protected)**

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Logged out successfully"
}
```

### GET `/auth/session`
Get current user session. **(Protected)**

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "user": {
    "uid": "user_id",
    "email": "user@example.com"
  }
}
```

---

## 👤 User Endpoints

### GET `/users/profile`
Get current user's profile. **(Protected)**

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "user": {
    "id": "user_id",
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "displayName": "John Doe",
    "role": "user",
    "credits": 100
  }
}
```

### PUT `/users/profile`
Update current user's profile. **(Protected)**

**Request:**
```json
{
  "displayName": "Jane Doe",
  "bio": "Software developer"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "user": { /* updated user */ }
}
```

### GET `/users/:id`
Get user by ID. **(Protected)**

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "user": { /* user object */ }
}
```

### PUT `/users/:id`
Update user by ID. **(Protected)**

**Request:**
```json
{
  "displayName": "Updated Name"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "user": { /* updated user */ }
}
```

### GET `/users/credits`
Get user's credits balance. **(Protected)**

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "credits": 100
}
```

---

## 📁 Project Endpoints

### GET `/projects`
Get all user's projects. **(Protected)**

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "projects": [
    {
      "id": "project_id",
      "name": "My Project",
      "description": "Project description",
      "userId": "user_id",
      "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

**WebSocket:** Automatically updated via `project:created/updated/deleted` events

### POST `/projects`
Create a new project. **(Protected)**

**Request:**
```json
{
  "name": "New Project",
  "description": "Project description"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "project": {
    "id": "project_id",
    "name": "New Project",
    "description": "Project description",
    "userId": "user_id",
    "createdAt": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"
  }
}
```

**WebSocket:** Emits `project:created` event to user

### GET `/projects/:id`
Get project by ID. **(Protected)**

**Response:**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "project": { /* project object */ }
